1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,769
Can a payments product be P C I D S S compliant on its own?

2
00:00:05,819 --> 00:00:10,000
Picture a bank that buys a product whose brochure says compliant.

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:19,230
The assessor asks for the firewall rules, the login logs, the people who hold the keys, and the camera footage of the server room.

4
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:26,153
The vendor has none of them, because those belong to the bank's whole building, not to one room.

5
00:00:26,203 --> 00:00:33,076
Worse, nobody wrote down which jobs are the product's and which are the bank's, so some fall between.

6
00:00:33,126 --> 00:00:39,230
Lesson four gave the answer: we deliver the locked room, and the bank owns the building.

7
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:41,538
So each unit ships a guide.

8
00:00:41,588 --> 00:00:48,076
It says what the bank's building must provide, how to install the room, and who does what.

9
00:00:48,126 --> 00:00:50,769
Who does what is a responsibility matrix.

10
00:00:50,819 --> 00:01:01,153
For each of the twelve requirements in P C I D S S, it lists what the product does, what is the bank's, and what is shared.

11
00:01:01,203 --> 00:01:06,923
A product row says what the code does; it is not a claim of compliance.

12
00:01:06,973 --> 00:01:15,384
Take the network: the product opens only two doors, the bank builds the firewalls, and the list of allowed connections is shared.

13
00:01:15,434 --> 00:01:22,307
Take logging: the product keeps audit trails, and collecting and reviewing them every day is the bank's job.

14
00:01:22,357 --> 00:01:29,615
ecom has its own matrix, because it holds no card number, and gets the smaller check from lesson four.

15
00:01:29,665 --> 00:01:35,000
Then come the known gaps: where the product still falls short at this release.

16
00:01:35,050 --> 00:01:39,230
Each gap names what the bank does until it is fixed.

17
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:41,153
The product is not certified.

18
00:01:41,203 --> 00:01:47,692
The assessor is the person who judges the whole building, with the guide as the product's evidence.

19
00:01:47,742 --> 00:01:49,230
Now read the guide.

20
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:55,384
Its first lines say the zone is the bank's, and that the guide claims no compliance.

21
00:01:55,434 --> 00:01:59,999
Section eleven is the matrix: product, bank and shared, row by row.

22
00:02:00,049 --> 00:02:05,384
Physical security is all the bank's, and the dual control of keys is shared.

23
00:02:05,434 --> 00:02:11,153
Section twelve lists the known gaps, each with the bank's control until it is fixed.

24
00:02:11,203 --> 00:02:13,846
And the guide ships with every release.

25
00:02:13,896 --> 00:02:17,692
We deliver the locked room; the bank owns the building.

26
00:02:17,742 --> 00:02:23,846
That is the whole course: the shop, the locked room, and the building around them both.
